      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "scm_call1_evening_clear",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay=1 sf_surface=1 bl_pbl=1, radt = 30 min) dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF (module_esm_dump hooks inside SUBROUTINE RRTM after GASABS of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F; dump scm_ref2_1.json). RRTM has no standalone real64 driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. Inputs are the dumped RRTM column (PAVEL, TAVEL, COLDRY, COLH2O, COLCO2 of the 103-layer extended column); expected values are SETCOEF's outputs JP, JT, JT1, FAC00/10/01/11, FORFAC, SELFFAC, SELFFRAC, INDSELF, CO2MULT and the counts LAYTROP, LAYSWTCH, LAYLOW. SELFFAC/SELFFRAC/INDSELF are compared through the *_lower views (zero above LAYTROP) because SETCOEF leaves them unassigned there and the dump holds stale memory. The scheme is diagnostic (no time step). Regime: call 1, 19:00 UTC (12:34 LST), first radiation call, clear sky; tbound 288 K. Tolerances: measured against a NumPy replica the component's integer bins are exact; FAC00..FAC11 agree to 2.4e-6 of their maximum (real32 PREFLOG/TREF/ln), FORFAC to 1.5e-7, SELFFAC/SELFFRAC to 1.2e-7, CO2MULT to 1.4e-6 relative; tolerances 3-5x above: integers Linf abs 1e-9, weights Linf abs 1e-5, continuum factors Linf abs 1e-6 (SELFFRAC 5e-6, it spans -8.4..1), CO2MULT Linf abs 5e-7 (max 0.072), spot checks rel 1e-5 on FORFAC and CO2MULT and abs 1e-5 on FAC00/FAC01 (whose real32 values near a reference pressure are as small as 1.6e-3 with a 5e-4 relative error).",
          "parameter_overrides": {},
          "expression_template_imports": [
            {
              "ref": "./tests/setcoef_scm_call1_evening_clear_inputs.esm"
            }
          ],
